+- finding-source · {"version":1,"source":"inv-4ebdbb23-9aba-4f61-ae91-b4a977ad8e63/cluster-3","artifact":"reviews/inv-4ebdbb23-9aba-4f61-ae91-b4a977ad8e63/final-review-inv-4ebdbb23-9aba-4f61-ae91-b4a977ad8e63.cluster-3.md","kind":"final-review","verdict":"not ready (B1: on Hermes 0.22.1+ the secret-name filter blocks HERDR_THREADS_CONTINUITY_KEY, so a launcher's key never reaches the hook, and the README's remedy cannot work)","occurrences":[{"section":"Must fix before landing","position":1,"key":"B1 (Hermes gateway): on Hermes 0.22.1 and later `HERDR_THREADS_CONTINUITY_KEY` can never reach the hook, because `_travels` refuses any name containing `KEY` even when listed in `terminal.client_env_passthrough` (`agent/session_client_env.py:48-54`, `tools/code_execution_env.py:29`, recorded in this repo at `docs/research/2026-10-23-integration-alternatives/alternatives/cross-agent-teams-mcp-jtianling/hermes.md:145-147`), and `pane_env()` correctly drops the gateway's copy, so `integrations/hermes/__init__.py:38` and the instruction at `integrations/hermes/README.md:67` (repeated in `src/harness/hermes.rs` setup notes and `tests/fixtures/golden/help/setup.txt`) deliver nothing and a keyed Hermes clone in a restored pane gets a new seat or stays seatless; fix by carrying the key under a name that passes the filter (no `KEY`, `TOKEN`, `AUTH` and so on, for example renaming the variable before it ships, which changes the §4.5 name agreed with the graph session and so needs coordinating with it), or obtain a human scope change row excluding the Hermes gateway and correct the README and setup notes, since a spec-level accepted limit alone cannot lower B1.","text":"B1 (Hermes gateway): on Hermes 0.22.1 and later `HERDR_THREADS_CONTINUITY_KEY` can never reach the hook, because `_travels` refuses any name containing `KEY` even when listed in `terminal.client_env_passthrough` (`agent/session_client_env.py:48-54`, `tools/code_execution_env.py:29`, recorded in this repo at `docs/research/2026-10-23-integration-alternatives/alternatives/cross-agent-teams-mcp-jtianling/hermes.md:145-147`), and `pane_env()` correctly drops the gateway's copy, so `integrations/hermes/__init__.py:38` and the instruction at `integrations/hermes/README.md:67` (repeated in `src/harness/hermes.rs` setup notes and `tests/fixtures/golden/help/setup.txt`) deliver nothing and a keyed Hermes clone in a restored pane gets a new seat or stays seatless; fix by carrying the key under a name that passes the filter (no `KEY`, `TOKEN`, `AUTH` and so on, for example renaming the variable before it ships, which changes the §4.5 name agreed with the graph session and so needs coordinating with it), or obtain a human scope change row excluding the Hermes gateway and correct the README and setup notes, since a spec-level accepted limit alone cannot lower B1."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":1,"key":"No live Hermes ran: `hermes` is not installed here, and the upstream policy was read from source at v0.22.7, plus the secret list at v0.22.1 (`session_client_env.py` at v0.22.1 could not be fetched in this pass). An attempt to execute the upstream module against the variable name was refused by the permission layer, so the filter behaviour is source-read and not executed.","text":"No live Hermes ran: `hermes` is not installed here, and the upstream policy was read from source at v0.22.7, plus the secret list at v0.22.1 (`session_client_env.py` at v0.22.1 could not be fetched in this pass). An attempt to execute the upstream module against the variable name was refused by the permission layer, so the filter behaviour is source-read and not executed."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":2,"key":"`test_gateway_child_takes_the_session_continuity_key_not_the_gateway_key` (`integrations/hermes/test_bridge.py:480`) stubs `bound_client_env`, so nothing in the suite exercises Hermes' real client-env filter; a regression test should assert the chosen variable name passes `_SECRET_SUBSTRIN